WEBVTT

00:15.724 --> 00:17.934
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:26.735 --> 00:29.612
EPISODE 9

00:29.696 --> 00:30.530
Hi.

00:32.365 --> 00:33.950
You wore your surgical cap to work?

00:35.452 --> 00:36.619
You should take your bib off.

00:37.454 --> 00:38.455
Hey, this is…

00:39.748 --> 00:41.875
Look at this. I knew this would happen.

00:41.958 --> 00:44.377
"Born in 1996.
Horoscope for second week of October."

00:44.461 --> 00:46.337
"A week of war
with fights breaking out often."

00:46.921 --> 00:49.841
"Especially with superiors at work,
they're strewn like landmines."

00:49.924 --> 00:51.676
"You can try, but you can't avoid them."

00:52.719 --> 00:55.930
Last week, you said things would be rosy,
but it was a battlefield for me.

00:56.014 --> 00:57.265
That's the problem.

00:57.348 --> 00:59.476
If that was supposed to be rosy,
imagine this week.

00:59.559 --> 01:01.853
There were 690,000 babies born in 1996.

01:01.936 --> 01:04.481
But it doesn't make sense
they'd all have the same fate.

01:04.564 --> 01:05.565
I don't believe in that.

01:05.648 --> 01:07.275
This is super accurate.

01:07.358 --> 01:08.193
Look.

01:08.693 --> 01:10.195
"Struggling without being fulfilled--"

01:12.405 --> 01:14.908
Geez, I'm just trying
to tell you to be careful.

01:19.704 --> 01:20.789
Excuse me.

01:36.805 --> 01:37.889
Hi.

01:39.390 --> 01:40.475
Hello.

01:46.314 --> 01:47.148
You're early.

01:47.982 --> 01:48.817
Yes.

01:55.115 --> 01:56.407
Then, want some coffee?

01:58.451 --> 01:59.661
Not on an empty stomach.

01:59.744 --> 02:02.080
Same. And I feel just as awkward
with you guys too.

02:02.163 --> 02:03.581
No, that's not what I meant.

02:03.665 --> 02:05.708
My stomach really is weak.

02:07.210 --> 02:08.336
It's the truth though.

02:08.419 --> 02:09.504
Hello, Professor Seo.

02:10.130 --> 02:12.632
Dr. Tak. I haven't seen you in a while.

02:12.715 --> 02:14.676
-How are you?
-Good.

02:15.552 --> 02:18.096
-Are you on Pediatrics rotation now?
-Yes.

02:18.680 --> 02:22.767
Seeing babies there every day
reminds me of my time in OB.

02:22.851 --> 02:26.229
It's October now, so shouldn't you decide
on a department soon?

02:26.312 --> 02:27.564
I'm still thinking things over.

02:28.231 --> 02:29.691
I wanted to go into Surgery,

02:29.774 --> 02:32.610
but after working in Internal Medicine,
that was appealing too.

02:32.694 --> 02:35.989
In that case, you can choose
a department where you can do both.

02:38.158 --> 02:39.075
Like OB-GYN.

02:39.659 --> 02:43.204
Didn't Dr. Pyo tell you about that?

02:43.288 --> 02:44.455
I did.

02:44.539 --> 02:45.707
I did tell you, right?

02:46.875 --> 02:47.959
Yes.

02:48.042 --> 02:48.877
Good job.

02:50.461 --> 02:52.839
I heard Nam-kyung was very good to you.

02:56.342 --> 02:57.594
Yes, very.

02:58.177 --> 03:01.431
Wherever I went,
there weren't any doctors like Dr. Pyo.

03:03.433 --> 03:05.184
Right? There isn't.

03:09.480 --> 03:10.815
You should go since you're busy.

03:14.819 --> 03:17.947
I hope to see you
in our OB-GYN residents' lounge next year.

03:20.450 --> 03:21.659
Thank you.

03:27.415 --> 03:28.625
I guess he's not coming.

03:28.708 --> 03:30.877
That can't be. He clearly said he would.

03:32.045 --> 03:33.755
I thought we were getting one somehow.

03:34.547 --> 03:35.465
Darn it.

03:44.724 --> 03:45.767
You can go up first.

03:59.614 --> 04:02.825
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

04:02.909 --> 04:03.743
Filming?

04:04.285 --> 04:06.537
Yeah, the professor gave the okay.

04:07.455 --> 04:10.291
They want to see our everyday work lives.

04:11.167 --> 04:12.919
Just be yourself. Don't force anything.

04:13.670 --> 04:15.838
Really? I can just be myself?

04:17.966 --> 04:19.467
But maybe work a bit harder?

04:19.550 --> 04:20.551
Okay.

04:20.635 --> 04:22.845
I got consent
from the patients about filming

04:22.929 --> 04:24.889
and notified those
who didn't want to do it,

04:24.973 --> 04:25.848
so it should be fine.

04:25.932 --> 04:26.766
Okay.

04:28.601 --> 04:29.435
There they are.

04:29.519 --> 04:30.478
Thanks for helping.

04:33.106 --> 04:38.444
LABOR, DELIVERY ROOM
MATERNAL FETAL INTENSIVE CARE UNIT

04:46.828 --> 04:47.704
Hello.

04:48.663 --> 04:50.456
Goodness. Hello.

04:50.540 --> 04:52.250
I'm TV producer Jang Yung-suk.

04:52.333 --> 04:53.668
First-year resident Oh Yi-young.

04:53.751 --> 04:57.130
Nice to meet you. Gosh, this is where
my Mo-ne and Ma-ne were born.

04:57.213 --> 04:58.298
Goodness.

05:00.675 --> 05:01.551
Is that so?

05:02.343 --> 05:03.303
Yes.

05:03.386 --> 05:04.929
Shall we go then?

05:05.013 --> 05:05.888
Just a moment.

05:05.972 --> 05:07.390
I'm here today

05:07.473 --> 05:10.685
with a colleague of mine
who knows hospitals well.

05:11.185 --> 05:13.271
But why is he so late?

05:13.354 --> 05:14.397
Sorry!

05:16.816 --> 05:17.900
-Hello.
-Hello.

05:17.984 --> 05:19.527
This is our camera operator.

05:19.610 --> 05:20.778
-Hello.
-Hello.

05:22.071 --> 05:23.906
I went to the tenth floor,
thinking it was GYN.

05:23.990 --> 05:25.158
GYN?

05:25.241 --> 05:26.993
I'm sure I said come to OB-GYN.

05:27.076 --> 05:29.203
Here, OB is Obstetrics. GYN is Gynecology.

05:29.287 --> 05:31.539
Combined, they're called OB-GYN.

05:32.457 --> 05:34.625
I didn't ask that, did I?

05:34.709 --> 05:36.794
-Why were you late?
-I went to the tenth floor.

05:36.878 --> 05:39.881
Why would you go there?
I clearly told you to come to OB-GYN.

05:39.964 --> 05:41.215
GYN is also OB-GYN.

05:41.299 --> 05:43.009
Hey, I never said go to GYN.

05:43.092 --> 05:44.469
I said OB-GYN.

05:44.552 --> 05:46.137
Also, I don't even know what GYN is.

05:46.220 --> 05:48.681
Shouldn't you know
if you're shooting a show on OB-GYN?

05:48.765 --> 05:51.517
You can shoot a show
without knowing what GYN is, okay?

05:51.601 --> 05:53.728
After doing a few dramas,
you've become arrogant.

05:53.811 --> 05:54.812
Excuse me.

05:55.313 --> 05:56.898
I'm a bit busy.

05:57.648 --> 05:59.609
If you're going to fight,
we can do it next time.

05:59.692 --> 06:01.694
-No, we're sorry.
-No, we apologize.

06:01.778 --> 06:03.029
Let's go then.

06:03.112 --> 06:03.946
Okay.

06:07.492 --> 06:08.993
What was the name of the show?

06:09.786 --> 06:11.120
It's a new show.

06:11.204 --> 06:14.499
The title is Jang Yung-suk's Wee-oww.

06:16.501 --> 06:19.504
It's a reality variety show
set in a hospital.

06:19.587 --> 06:22.882
But a hospital isn't
as dramatic or tense every day

06:23.382 --> 06:26.094
as you might think it is.

06:26.594 --> 06:28.721
It's just a place
where people work and stay.

06:29.472 --> 06:30.306
Yes?

06:30.807 --> 06:31.641
What?

06:34.227 --> 06:36.145
Why is Dr. Myeong in an ambulance?

06:39.315 --> 06:40.316
AMBULANCE ONLY

06:40.399 --> 06:41.526
Please be careful.

06:42.527 --> 06:43.486
Name is Song Na-mu.

06:43.569 --> 06:45.988
She's 38 weeks, elderly primi,
and ROM with contractions.

06:46.072 --> 06:49.367
She's not our patient,
but she's in pain and lives far away.

06:49.450 --> 06:51.160
-So let's admit her.
-Okay.

07:07.969 --> 07:09.053
-Excuse me?
-Yes?

07:09.137 --> 07:09.971
That's

07:11.013 --> 07:11.848
mine.

07:11.931 --> 07:13.766
-I see.
-Thank you.

07:18.062 --> 07:22.150
How could I ignore a mother
whose water just broke?

07:23.192 --> 07:25.945
She was lucky though.

07:26.904 --> 07:29.866
She was in shock,
so while being transported…

07:29.949 --> 07:32.660
She came in with the mother
who fainted at the department store?

07:32.743 --> 07:35.413
Yes. And it was in front of film crew
on their first day here.

07:35.496 --> 07:36.789
Right place, right time.

07:36.873 --> 07:38.791
So that's why she's being interviewed.

07:38.875 --> 07:40.001
Yes.

07:40.084 --> 07:44.213
But why was Dr. Myeong
at a department store during work hours?

07:45.256 --> 07:47.925
Nurse, serology and blood typing
were sent out, right?

07:48.009 --> 07:48.843
Yes.

07:50.928 --> 07:53.264
I'll check Ms. Lee Mi-ju's
amniotic fluid and ultrasound.

07:53.764 --> 07:55.600
Dr. Myeong said she'd do that…

07:55.683 --> 07:56.726
She told me to do it.

07:57.351 --> 07:59.228
I'll do just these two
and check on Ms. Song.

07:59.937 --> 08:01.022
Okay.

08:03.065 --> 08:04.484
I'm Professor Kong Gi-sun.

08:04.567 --> 08:06.652
-You must've been pretty startled.
-Yes.

08:07.945 --> 08:09.989
I had labor induction
scheduled for next week,

08:10.072 --> 08:12.783
so I didn't expect my water
would break before then.

08:12.867 --> 08:14.577
I see.

08:15.286 --> 08:17.163
Since you said you'll give birth here,

08:17.246 --> 08:20.416
I've contacted your hospital
in Haenam myself

08:20.500 --> 08:22.418
and retrieved your medical records.

08:22.502 --> 08:27.256
I went ahead and checked
your lab results myself today,

08:27.340 --> 08:28.925
and everything looks just fine.

08:30.468 --> 08:32.803
That's such a relief.
Thank you, Professor.

08:33.888 --> 08:36.349
I do have many deliveries lined up, but…

08:37.767 --> 08:38.976
I see.

08:40.102 --> 08:42.813
Then, can the doctor who saved me

08:43.314 --> 08:44.690
deliver my baby?

08:47.235 --> 08:49.362
Do you mean Dr. Myeong?

08:49.445 --> 08:50.571
Yes.

08:51.405 --> 08:52.615
There's no need.

08:52.698 --> 08:55.785
Professor Kong is much more skilled
at deliveries than I am.

08:55.868 --> 08:58.746
It just feels like
the way we met was fate.

08:59.664 --> 09:03.209
If you could deliver my baby as well,
I won't ever forget you.

09:06.754 --> 09:08.631
I think that would be a good idea as well.

09:09.840 --> 09:12.552
I'm busy anyway.

09:13.344 --> 09:14.428
Take good care of her.

09:15.346 --> 09:16.514
Okay, then.

09:19.100 --> 09:20.393
Doctor!

09:20.476 --> 09:22.353
I'll do my best.

09:22.436 --> 09:24.522
Of course. I'll put my full trust in you.

09:24.605 --> 09:25.565
Thank you.

09:28.192 --> 09:30.611
-Don't worry.
-Thank you.

09:36.534 --> 09:38.244
She came to Seoul to see a fortune teller.

09:38.327 --> 09:41.163
They said a natural birth
was essential for the baby's health.

09:43.416 --> 09:44.625
Prep with that in mind.

09:45.376 --> 09:47.753
But, Doctor,
the patient is on the older side,

09:47.837 --> 09:49.755
and her pelvic outlet is a bit narrow.

09:49.839 --> 09:51.424
The EBW is on the heavier side too.

09:51.507 --> 09:52.341
Really?

09:53.884 --> 09:56.429
If it's 3.5 kg, it's still fine.

09:56.512 --> 09:57.513
You scared me.

09:58.598 --> 10:00.850
I promised her a VD.

10:01.434 --> 10:04.937
But what if that doesn't go smoothly
and we have to operate?

10:05.021 --> 10:06.439
I've seen a lot of cases like that.

10:06.522 --> 10:07.940
Don't you think I know that?

10:08.441 --> 10:09.567
But we have to.

10:10.276 --> 10:12.737
I guaranteed her
a natural delivery on camera.

10:12.820 --> 10:14.196
I'll look foolish if we operate.

10:14.280 --> 10:15.239
What?

10:15.323 --> 10:18.075
It even won't be a tall order.
Let's make it a natural delivery.

10:21.412 --> 10:22.246
Okay.

10:22.747 --> 10:25.124
I was too busy to buy you a coffee today.

10:25.207 --> 10:26.042
-Hello.
-Hello.

10:26.125 --> 10:27.460
I'm sorry.

10:28.169 --> 10:31.922
It's okay. You haven't even eaten yet.
Your lunch box was still there.

10:32.006 --> 10:34.050
No wonder why I felt so hungry.

10:35.718 --> 10:38.220
Jae-il, the intern coming to GYN tomorrow

10:38.304 --> 10:39.347
is Nam Dong-eun, right?

10:39.430 --> 10:41.599
Yes, I told him to come right to the ward.

10:42.308 --> 10:43.809
I heard from a friend

10:43.893 --> 10:46.145
that he's had rotations
with eight departments

10:46.854 --> 10:48.773
and went to work dinners
with seven of them.

10:49.482 --> 10:51.567
He's like me then. Very extroverted.

10:51.651 --> 10:53.027
No, that's not it.

10:53.527 --> 10:56.322
In all seven
of the work dinners he went to,

10:57.490 --> 10:59.408
they had beef barbecue.

11:00.701 --> 11:03.496
And that means he must obviously be…

11:03.579 --> 11:04.830
-perfect!
-Perfect!

11:05.831 --> 11:07.875
I wish someone like that
would join our department.

11:07.958 --> 11:09.210
Doctor.

11:10.044 --> 11:10.961
Don't you worry.

11:11.462 --> 11:12.713
I might not know everything,

11:13.214 --> 11:15.216
but I know how to steal someone's heart.

11:15.299 --> 11:18.469
I've stolen the hearts of every fan,
from young girls to their moms.

11:19.178 --> 11:20.388
Convicted 124 times for theft,

11:21.180 --> 11:24.433
I'm the bandit known as Um Jay.

11:27.895 --> 11:28.729
Hey.

11:29.563 --> 11:30.398
Hello, sir.

11:31.273 --> 11:32.900
I clearly told you on Friday

11:32.983 --> 11:35.236
to call Colorectal Surgery
for a co-op consult, didn't I?

11:35.319 --> 11:36.654
Yes, sir. You did.

11:41.826 --> 11:45.079
But they're all going to a conference
on Friday, so no one will be here.

11:45.162 --> 11:46.247
Sir, I--

11:46.914 --> 11:49.208
I'm sorry, Professor.
I'll do whatever I can to book it.

11:49.291 --> 11:50.376
There's no need.

11:51.001 --> 11:51.836
Why?

11:51.919 --> 11:52.920
Because I booked it.

11:53.003 --> 11:56.298
The professor arranged
the consult himself.

11:57.133 --> 12:00.386
What kind of third-year goes around
forgetting to book consults?

12:01.137 --> 12:02.888
Even first-years don't make that mistake.

12:02.972 --> 12:06.183
What on earth could he
possibly learn from you? What?!

12:07.893 --> 12:08.727
Wait, sir…

12:08.811 --> 12:09.979
I'm sorry.

12:10.062 --> 12:12.273
You prepare for surgery like a damn…

12:16.026 --> 12:18.028
Geez. Seriously.

12:24.410 --> 12:25.619
I'm sorry, Doctor.

12:26.912 --> 12:28.414
You told me to do it yesterday.

12:30.583 --> 12:31.500
I know.

12:35.045 --> 12:35.880
I…

12:42.344 --> 12:43.929
I should've checked once more.

12:44.513 --> 12:45.598
Right?

12:45.681 --> 12:46.807
I forgot too.

12:48.517 --> 12:50.978
No, it was my mistake.

12:51.061 --> 12:52.354
Because of me…

12:54.940 --> 12:55.983
I'm sorry, Doctor.

12:56.066 --> 12:59.945
If you know you messed up, it's okay.
Just don't make the same mistake again.

13:01.530 --> 13:02.364
Yes, Doctor.

13:02.907 --> 13:05.284
I won't ever make this mistake again.
I promise.

13:08.412 --> 13:09.288
Doctor Ki.

13:10.664 --> 13:11.582
I'm very sorry.

13:11.665 --> 13:13.125
I get it. It's fine.

13:13.209 --> 13:14.919
I'll go explain the surgery for Room 1004.

13:15.461 --> 13:16.295
Okay.

13:21.091 --> 13:24.178
I guess this is why
everyone calls her Eun-mi the Saint.

13:25.221 --> 13:26.555
Imagine if it was Dr. Cha.

13:28.140 --> 13:30.768
I didn't see the lab update in the notes.

13:30.851 --> 13:31.977
I'll get to it, ma'am.

13:32.061 --> 13:34.939
And I saw we switched
Jang Jin-gyeong's pain meds to fentanyl.

13:35.022 --> 13:36.106
I saw that too!

13:39.652 --> 13:42.321
If a first-year makes a mistake,
the second-year gets blamed,

13:42.404 --> 13:43.489
so I was nervous about it.

13:43.572 --> 13:44.823
But I didn't make a mistake…

13:48.202 --> 13:50.663
Thank you for checking
despite your busy schedule.

13:52.623 --> 13:55.292
Right, so to make sure
I don't have to worry,

13:55.376 --> 13:56.877
let's do better, okay?

13:58.587 --> 13:59.421
Yes, ma'am.

14:00.589 --> 14:01.507
But, Doctor,

14:01.590 --> 14:04.093
I'm organizing
this week's surgery schedule.

14:04.677 --> 14:06.679
The PDS planned
for Ms. Kwon Yu-jin on Thursday

14:06.762 --> 14:09.098
was canceled
and was changed to an IDS instead.

14:09.181 --> 14:10.015
Why is that so?

14:10.099 --> 14:12.893
We were told to do that.

14:12.977 --> 14:13.811
Right.

14:15.354 --> 14:18.065
But when Ms. Park Seong-ok
had surgery last week,

14:18.148 --> 14:21.151
serous carcinoma was suspected on her CT,

14:21.235 --> 14:23.946
and the level of METs was similar,
but we still went with PDS.

14:24.029 --> 14:26.448
Right, so the professor told us to…

14:27.032 --> 14:28.158
Yes, I'll be right there!

14:29.410 --> 14:31.328
I'm busy right now. We'll talk later.

14:35.249 --> 14:37.042
Geez, that darn "second-year"!

14:37.126 --> 14:40.087
-Dr. Cha?
-Yeah, she calls every hour.

14:40.629 --> 14:42.339
"Did you do it? Are you going to?"

14:42.423 --> 14:43.966
She's gotten much better.

14:44.049 --> 14:45.551
She used to call me every 30 minutes.

14:45.634 --> 14:47.761
She never answers my questions.

14:48.429 --> 14:50.264
I'm the one who can't trust her.

14:50.347 --> 14:53.726
Hey, someone with separation anxiety
and trust issues is still better

14:54.935 --> 14:57.271
than a slacker senior
who always steals the credit.

14:58.731 --> 15:00.024
Dr. Myeong?

15:00.816 --> 15:01.901
Yeah.

15:02.610 --> 15:03.944
Or maybe not?

15:04.028 --> 15:05.446
Is that one better?

15:06.071 --> 15:08.157
No. They're all weird in OB-GYN.

15:08.782 --> 15:09.700
That is true.

15:10.326 --> 15:11.827
My anesthesiologist friend told me

15:11.911 --> 15:14.872
watching an OB surgery
is like watching a horror film.

15:15.456 --> 15:18.167
When we're delivering the baby,
everyone's shouting and yelling.

15:18.250 --> 15:20.377
As soon as the baby's out,
we start humming happily.

15:20.961 --> 15:23.589
By the time we're closing up,
we ask in the kindest voice,

15:23.672 --> 15:25.257
"Where do you live?"

15:25.341 --> 15:26.675
"Have you eaten yet?"

15:27.635 --> 15:30.179
All of this happening within three minutes

15:30.262 --> 15:31.680
makes it super creepy.

15:32.640 --> 15:33.807
No one's normal.

15:33.891 --> 15:35.809
No, there is one person who's normal.

15:36.518 --> 15:37.728
Who?

15:38.520 --> 15:39.396
Dr. Ki Eun-mi.

15:39.480 --> 15:40.898
Yeah, I agree with that.

15:41.899 --> 15:45.361
Did you know Dr. Ki is of mixed ancestry?

15:46.654 --> 15:49.740
She was born half-human, half-angel.

15:49.823 --> 15:51.784
That's why her blood type is angel type.

15:52.701 --> 15:55.204
And starting from today,
she's my role model.

15:55.788 --> 15:57.748
Second only in admiration
to my colleagues, BTS,

15:57.831 --> 16:00.250
she's my hero, savior, and mentor.

16:01.627 --> 16:03.379
There's one more normal person.

16:04.129 --> 16:05.255
Dr. Ku Do-won.

16:06.298 --> 16:08.050
-Right.
-What are you talking about?

16:08.133 --> 16:10.970
Mr. Routine voluntarily shows up early
every day at 4:30 a.m.

16:11.053 --> 16:12.262
You think that's normal?

16:12.346 --> 16:13.472
He doesn't anymore.

16:14.431 --> 16:16.141
He sometimes gets in at 6:00 a.m.

16:16.225 --> 16:17.643
How do you know that?

16:17.726 --> 16:18.602
I saw him.

16:19.812 --> 16:20.813
What?

16:20.896 --> 16:22.815
I mean, I didn't see him.

16:25.317 --> 16:27.027
Sometimes, he wasn't in the cafeteria.

16:28.445 --> 16:29.613
At 5:00 a.m.

16:29.697 --> 16:32.408
Mr. Routine has changed.
He used to be my role model.

16:32.491 --> 16:34.076
How many role models do you have?

16:36.036 --> 16:37.496
OH JOO-YOUNG

16:39.289 --> 16:40.791
-I have to go.
-Where?

16:42.042 --> 16:43.002
To have dinner.

16:43.085 --> 16:44.378
You were just eating!

16:54.722 --> 16:55.556
Seung-won.

16:56.181 --> 16:57.057
What?

17:03.564 --> 17:04.440
I…

17:06.608 --> 17:07.443
What is it?

17:12.322 --> 17:13.365
Yi-young…

17:18.454 --> 17:19.913
Don't fight with her.

17:24.209 --> 17:25.961
Sweetie! Honey!

17:26.045 --> 17:26.879
Sweetie!

17:30.549 --> 17:32.843
-What's this? You bought groceries?
-Yeah.

17:32.926 --> 17:34.011
-Like what?
-What you asked.

17:34.094 --> 17:36.597
-Let me see.
-Kiwis and loach soup.

17:36.680 --> 17:38.265
I don't like loach soup though.

17:38.348 --> 17:40.267
I didn't buy this for you.

17:41.769 --> 17:43.020
And the oranges?

17:44.188 --> 17:45.773
I really don't like loach soup.

17:47.399 --> 17:48.817
-Hey, be careful!
-It's hot!

17:50.694 --> 17:51.653
Really, Seung-won?

17:51.737 --> 17:53.989
Sorry, love is an involuntary reflex.

17:54.656 --> 17:55.783
I couldn't help it.

17:55.866 --> 17:57.493
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

18:03.957 --> 18:06.168
I'm carrying a life. Remember?

18:07.294 --> 18:08.754
Please be careful around me.

18:09.671 --> 18:12.174
You just had the embryo transfer today.
It's still a cell.

18:12.257 --> 18:14.426
How dare you refer to our Forever as "it"?

18:15.010 --> 18:16.386
"For" what?

18:16.470 --> 18:18.847
You take "young" from Joo-young
and "won" from Seung-won,

18:18.931 --> 18:21.266
and you get "young-won" or forever.

18:22.351 --> 18:23.936
What do you think?
Good nickname, right?

18:24.937 --> 18:26.730
What a cheesy nickname.

18:27.397 --> 18:29.066
Did you have trouble with anything today?

18:29.149 --> 18:30.984
I was so happy I couldn't tell.

18:31.068 --> 18:33.362
There were four embryos this time.

18:33.445 --> 18:36.406
Two were transplanted and two were frozen,
so we could try again.

18:37.074 --> 18:38.992
It's like a savings plan.
It's so reassuring.

18:39.493 --> 18:42.621
I thought no more egg retrievals
meant no more shots, so I was happy.

18:42.704 --> 18:43.872
But now it's a different one.

18:43.956 --> 18:45.624
-Shots?
-Yeah.

18:46.458 --> 18:48.335
Shots to thicken the uterine lining.

18:48.418 --> 18:51.171
It helps with implantation
and chances of maintaining the pregnancy.

18:53.215 --> 18:54.174
But it hurts a lot.

18:54.716 --> 18:55.551
Why?

18:55.634 --> 18:57.136
They're progesterone shots,

18:57.219 --> 18:58.637
but unlike the others,

18:58.720 --> 19:01.640
it's oil-based and causes hard lumps
at the injection site.

19:01.723 --> 19:03.433
So they're nicknamed "rock injections."

19:04.726 --> 19:06.478
You know more than our first-years do.

19:07.062 --> 19:09.481
Well, I've got IVF experience
under my belt.

19:09.982 --> 19:12.985
Hey, first-year,
just come to me with your questions.

19:14.987 --> 19:18.115
Stop eating that and eat proper food.
You said you wanted loach soup.

19:18.198 --> 19:21.034
She said avocados, kiwis,
and loach soup are good for implantation,

19:21.118 --> 19:22.619
so we bought a week's worth.

19:23.453 --> 19:25.289
Just having a balanced diet will do.

19:25.914 --> 19:26.832
Yeah.

19:26.915 --> 19:28.083
See? That's enough of this.

19:28.167 --> 19:29.459
Gosh, it's too cold.

19:29.543 --> 19:30.836
Have some hot loach soup.

19:32.045 --> 19:33.213
You're so funny.

19:34.006 --> 19:35.757
Did I tell you about our trip?

19:35.841 --> 19:37.092
A trip? All of a sudden?

19:37.176 --> 19:39.970
We have to wait over a week
to find out if implantation worked.

19:40.053 --> 19:42.181
We thought of doing something
to pass the time faster.

19:42.264 --> 19:43.640
Well, if I stay home,

19:43.724 --> 19:47.227
I'd stare at the pregnancy test all day
and get stressed about it.

19:47.311 --> 19:50.314
She promised me
she won't do any tests this time.

19:51.773 --> 19:52.900
That's great.

19:52.983 --> 19:54.818
Have fun and enjoy a change in scenery.

19:56.862 --> 19:57.946
Can you hand me my phone?

20:04.244 --> 20:05.245
PREGNANCY TEST KIT

20:18.425 --> 20:19.426
Hello?

20:19.509 --> 20:21.511
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

20:32.606 --> 20:34.441
Would you like to think it over?

20:34.524 --> 20:36.151
No, I'll do it.

20:36.735 --> 20:37.861
Okay. Then--

20:37.945 --> 20:39.821
Wait, I don't think I can do it.

20:40.656 --> 20:42.491
Okay. Then we'll just forget about--

20:42.574 --> 20:44.701
No, I'll do it. Please sign me up.

20:45.869 --> 20:47.204
You made a good choice.

20:48.038 --> 20:51.333
It's an installment savings plan
for young to middle-aged adults.

20:51.416 --> 20:53.502
It's 150,000 won per month
for a year. Correct?

20:53.585 --> 20:54.419
Yes.

20:56.672 --> 21:00.008
We also have two-year plans.
Would you like to hear about them?

21:00.092 --> 21:01.593
No, I need the money next year.

21:02.094 --> 21:03.929
I might become an aunt by then.

21:06.348 --> 21:09.518
I wanted to buy an infant car seat,
but it was so expensive.

21:09.601 --> 21:11.728
So you're going to be an aunt.

21:11.812 --> 21:13.313
Congratulations in advance.

21:13.397 --> 21:14.314
Is it a boy or a girl?

21:14.398 --> 21:17.317
We don't know yet. It's still just a cell.

21:18.318 --> 21:21.363
But whatever it may, I'll be happy.

21:22.030 --> 21:23.907
It sounds like you
and your sister are close.

21:24.533 --> 21:26.576
We're really not. She hates me.

21:28.078 --> 21:30.163
I hope you see
the plan through until the end.

21:35.210 --> 21:36.044
Excuse me,

21:36.712 --> 21:39.172
I have a question.

21:41.008 --> 21:43.010
To extend my overdraft account next year…

21:43.093 --> 21:44.886
We just need your proof of employment.

21:46.638 --> 21:47.723
And if I don't have that?

21:47.806 --> 21:49.266
That might make it hard.

21:50.600 --> 21:51.435
Right.

21:55.647 --> 21:57.357
What brings you to the bank?

21:58.608 --> 22:00.485
Well… Nothing, really.

22:03.030 --> 22:03.864
Here.

22:07.659 --> 22:08.994
I already had breakfast though.

22:09.077 --> 22:10.829
No, it's not for you.

22:13.623 --> 22:15.500
Your sister likes the streusel bread here.

22:15.584 --> 22:18.211
But I'm stuck here today.
Could you give it to her?

22:20.547 --> 22:22.215
I like streusel bread too.

22:23.508 --> 22:25.427
Even more than my sister.

22:32.684 --> 22:34.561
I'll buy you some next time.

22:34.644 --> 22:36.146
That's what you always say.

22:36.980 --> 22:38.273
You said you'd buy me crabs too.

22:40.275 --> 22:41.651
They're just empty promises, right?

22:43.153 --> 22:43.987
Look at this.

22:44.071 --> 22:45.363
You forgot, didn't you?

22:49.117 --> 22:50.327
Dr. Oh, I…

23:00.378 --> 23:02.297
Would you like to have dinner with me?

23:06.885 --> 23:08.512
-Tomorrow at 9:00 p.m.?
-Okay.

23:09.554 --> 23:10.972
Shouldn't you check your schedule--

23:11.056 --> 23:12.974
I'm free. Absolutely…

23:14.976 --> 23:15.811
I can make it.

23:25.195 --> 23:26.363
Your phone.

23:28.198 --> 23:29.032
What should we eat?

23:32.869 --> 23:34.496
-Your phone.
-Where should we go?

23:43.380 --> 23:44.214
Dr. Oh.

23:46.341 --> 23:47.217
Your phone.

23:47.300 --> 23:48.135
Right.

23:51.930 --> 23:52.806
Yes?

23:53.557 --> 23:54.641
I'll be right there.

24:08.488 --> 24:09.781
I'm almost there, Sa-bi.

24:11.074 --> 24:12.075
Me too.

24:15.370 --> 24:16.413
What's going on?

24:16.496 --> 24:17.372
Doctor.

24:17.873 --> 24:21.960
The professor asked me
to remove the drainage bag.

24:22.043 --> 24:23.044
Okay.

24:24.880 --> 24:26.006
The Number 1 bag.

24:30.135 --> 24:31.803
What did you just remove?

24:31.887 --> 24:33.138
I'm sorry.

24:33.221 --> 24:34.139
Being sorry doesn't--

24:34.222 --> 24:35.724
Our intern didn't know--

24:35.807 --> 24:37.475
We should've been here with him.

24:38.059 --> 24:38.977
I'm sorry.

24:40.270 --> 24:41.229
Then what do we do?

24:41.897 --> 24:43.857
Won't this cause problems?

24:43.940 --> 24:46.359
Yesterday, the Number 1 bag
barely had any drainage,

24:46.443 --> 24:49.070
so the professor said
to remove it first this morning.

24:49.654 --> 24:53.408
The Number 2 bag also has barely had
any drainage since yesterday afternoon.

24:53.491 --> 24:56.203
The color and volume
in the bags look fine,

24:56.286 --> 24:58.371
so removing both should be fine.

24:58.455 --> 25:00.373
There's nothing to worry about now.

25:01.124 --> 25:03.460
Really? It's okay?

25:05.086 --> 25:08.006
Still, we'll let the professor know

25:08.089 --> 25:10.717
and check when the remaining bag
can be removed

25:10.800 --> 25:11.760
and we'll let you know.

25:11.843 --> 25:14.679
So you're saying she's okay?

25:14.763 --> 25:15.597
Yes.

25:16.765 --> 25:18.225
We're sorry for alarming you.

25:19.017 --> 25:20.185
I was so scared.

25:20.852 --> 25:22.270
Please make sure and ask.

25:22.354 --> 25:23.521
Of course.

25:25.899 --> 25:26.942
I'm sorry.

25:27.025 --> 25:28.109
Right.

25:29.778 --> 25:30.737
We'll let you rest.

25:40.538 --> 25:41.748
Dr. Nam.

25:41.831 --> 25:43.875
Why did you call us both? We're busy.

25:46.628 --> 25:49.631
I called you first, but you didn't answer.

25:50.757 --> 25:52.968
So I called him,
and he said he'd come right away.

25:53.760 --> 25:56.554
But then, you said you were coming too.

25:57.138 --> 25:59.307
I usually don't get angry
at anyone so easily.

25:59.391 --> 26:01.268
But why do you keep making
ridiculous mistakes?

26:01.351 --> 26:03.979
And it's all on the chart. So why?!

26:05.981 --> 26:07.148
It can happen.

26:07.232 --> 26:09.442
Today's his first day at GYN,
so it's hectic for him.

26:10.026 --> 26:10.860
Right?

26:12.028 --> 26:14.281
I'll call the professor and find out.

26:15.699 --> 26:16.825
Thank you.

26:17.993 --> 26:18.994
Have you had lunch yet?

26:22.956 --> 26:24.916
Get yourself some coffee and snacks.

26:25.709 --> 26:27.127
And get some fresh air too.

26:29.671 --> 26:31.006
Thank you.

26:31.089 --> 26:31.965
Go on.

26:32.674 --> 26:33.508
It's okay.

26:36.052 --> 26:38.930
Hey, you have to tell him
exactly what he did wrong.

26:39.014 --> 26:41.683
He probably knew what to do,
but was just too nervous.

26:44.728 --> 26:46.813
Are you trying to lure him over to OB-GYN?

26:46.896 --> 26:49.607
No. I'm trying to copy what Dr. Ki does.

26:49.691 --> 26:50.900
Just copying her won't work.

26:52.986 --> 26:53.862
Excuse me.

26:53.945 --> 26:55.363
Yes? How can we help you?

26:55.447 --> 26:57.115
Are you, by any chance…

26:57.782 --> 26:58.616
Excuse me.

27:01.745 --> 27:04.039
-Yes?
-You're him, aren't you?

27:04.664 --> 27:06.291
-It's you, right?
-Sorry?

27:07.083 --> 27:08.084
HI-BOYZ!

27:09.461 --> 27:10.879
You're Um Jay, right?

27:10.962 --> 27:12.047
Yes.

27:26.269 --> 27:28.021
How did you recognize me?

27:28.104 --> 27:31.232
I've been a huge fan of yours
since middle school.

27:32.192 --> 27:35.195
I cried so much when you disbanded.

27:36.529 --> 27:38.239
You debuted on February 4, 2011.

27:38.323 --> 27:40.158
Your first music show win
was on June 2, 2012.

27:40.241 --> 27:42.660
And you suddenly disbanded
on December 28, 2013.

27:45.955 --> 27:46.790
Jay.

27:49.959 --> 27:51.127
Thank you.

27:53.046 --> 27:55.465
Your mother will be fine.

27:55.548 --> 27:57.634
Yes, I think she will.

28:00.970 --> 28:02.472
-Are you okay?
-Yes.

28:03.807 --> 28:04.808
Doctor.

28:05.767 --> 28:06.601
Have some tea.

28:07.185 --> 28:08.269
Thank you.

28:16.403 --> 28:17.946
Is something wrong with Ms. Song?

28:18.029 --> 28:20.615
No, she removed the NST
to go to the bathroom.

28:20.698 --> 28:22.158
I helped her put it back on.

28:22.242 --> 28:23.410
When did you examine her?

28:23.493 --> 28:25.412
Three hours ago, and she was at 2.5 cm.

28:25.495 --> 28:26.496
And the ultrasound?

28:26.996 --> 28:29.040
I checked yesterday
when she came and it was fine.

28:29.958 --> 28:31.167
Then check it again now.

28:32.252 --> 28:33.461
What? Why?

28:33.545 --> 28:34.963
Tell Ms. Song

28:35.046 --> 28:36.923
that I especially asked you to check.

28:37.006 --> 28:38.758
I'm going into surgery, so text me.

28:38.842 --> 28:41.469
Surgery? You don't have any today.

28:42.429 --> 28:43.596
I'm assisting.

28:43.680 --> 28:44.681
Go check now.

28:45.765 --> 28:46.599
Okay.

28:49.686 --> 28:50.979
I'm going for an ultrasound.

28:51.604 --> 28:52.689
Okay.

28:55.275 --> 28:57.569
Ma'am, we'll put you under now.

28:57.652 --> 29:00.113
We'll put the injection in your back.

29:00.196 --> 29:03.450
You may be afraid since you can't see,
but it doesn't hurt too bad.

29:04.075 --> 29:06.828
I'll hold your hand.

29:11.374 --> 29:13.960
Please bend forward a little more.

29:17.714 --> 29:20.759
And lastly, don't forget
to remove the Foley catheter

29:20.842 --> 29:22.886
-from Ms. Yoo Ji-an tomorrow morning.
-Okay.

29:22.969 --> 29:24.387
If she can't self-void--

29:24.471 --> 29:26.681
We'll need to reinsert the Foley,
so I'll make sure.

29:29.934 --> 29:31.644
And this is really the last thing.

29:31.728 --> 29:34.481
Prescriptions and consent forms
for tomorrow's surgeries--

29:34.564 --> 29:35.690
Doctor?

29:35.774 --> 29:38.485
Ms. Oh Seol-eun's been vomiting,
so I asked for an antiemetic.

29:38.568 --> 29:40.487
Right. I'll prescribe it now.

29:40.570 --> 29:43.615
And the professor said to change
Ms. Kim Yoon-jin's anti-cancer drug.

29:43.698 --> 29:44.824
Right.

29:45.366 --> 29:46.242
You're right.

29:46.951 --> 29:50.497
Gosh, what was that anti-cancer drug?

29:51.164 --> 29:52.499
-Gemcitabine and carboplatin.
-Right.

29:57.378 --> 29:58.254
You got it right.

30:05.011 --> 30:06.054
But, Doctor,

30:06.846 --> 30:10.725
for patients on gemcitabine only,
we prescribed 1,000 per BSA.

30:11.518 --> 30:15.188
Is it right to use the same dose
when it's on a regimen with carboplatin?

30:15.271 --> 30:16.689
STRUCTURED TREATMENT PLAN

30:16.773 --> 30:18.775
Why don't you look it up before you ask?

30:18.858 --> 30:20.860
That'll help you study too.

30:21.861 --> 30:22.987
Yes, ma'am.

30:29.577 --> 30:31.079
We do use the same dosage.

30:31.162 --> 30:32.789
See? It is the same dosage.

30:34.040 --> 30:35.750
Try to remember these things.

30:35.834 --> 30:38.586
Don't ask because you forget again.

30:40.129 --> 30:40.964
Yes, ma'am.

30:43.132 --> 30:45.468
Is Ms. Song all right?

30:45.552 --> 30:47.971
She was in pain,
so I gave her a PCA an hour ago.

30:48.054 --> 30:49.389
She's better now.

30:50.390 --> 30:51.349
Ma'am!

30:54.727 --> 30:55.812
I'm sorry.

30:55.895 --> 30:57.355
Are they still filming?

30:57.438 --> 30:58.523
I think so.

30:58.606 --> 31:00.817
Damn, I'm at home.

31:01.484 --> 31:02.318
Then…

31:02.402 --> 31:04.654
I'll prepare Ms. Lee Yong-shim's
results for tomorrow--

31:04.737 --> 31:05.864
Wait.

31:05.947 --> 31:09.325
I think I need to see Ms. Song.

31:09.409 --> 31:12.161
What? You said you're at home.

31:12.245 --> 31:13.997
I am, but…

31:15.832 --> 31:16.958
I should go and see.

31:17.834 --> 31:18.668
Wait.

31:19.335 --> 31:20.169
Let's do this.

31:25.466 --> 31:26.551
What?

31:26.634 --> 31:32.307
MYEONG EUN-WON

31:32.390 --> 31:33.349
Hi, Dr. Oh.

31:38.688 --> 31:42.066
Ms. Song, I'm away right now
due to a paper I'm writing.

31:42.150 --> 31:43.526
But I was just worried.

31:43.610 --> 31:45.361
Despite the hassle, I hope you understand.

31:45.445 --> 31:47.405
You didn't have to call like this.

31:47.488 --> 31:49.991
I'm just so grateful. Thank you, Doctor.

31:50.074 --> 31:53.202
You're looking well.
Everything will be fine.

31:54.203 --> 31:58.166
I was in and out of pain all day.
It's a bit scary.

31:58.249 --> 32:01.210
I'm getting reports in real-time.

32:01.294 --> 32:03.963
If anything happens,
I'll be there even if it's late at night,

32:04.047 --> 32:05.006
so don't worry.

32:05.715 --> 32:06.841
Thank you.

32:06.925 --> 32:08.551
Dr. Oh.

32:08.635 --> 32:09.510
Yes?

32:10.511 --> 32:11.721
I can't see your face.

32:15.099 --> 32:16.726
-I'm here.
-Right.

32:16.809 --> 32:20.355
Monitor contractions and the baby
and text me every hour.

32:20.438 --> 32:21.314
Every hour?

32:21.397 --> 32:23.274
Yeah. Keep up the good work.

32:26.778 --> 32:29.489
My goodness. She's such an amazing doctor.

32:29.572 --> 32:30.657
I know, right?

32:32.325 --> 32:34.494
I'll be back in an hour then.

32:35.203 --> 32:36.037
Okay.

32:40.667 --> 32:41.501
Hello, Doctor.

32:41.584 --> 32:45.380
The intern's supposed to observe surgery,
but he's not here or picking up either.

32:46.464 --> 32:47.924
Let me try calling him.

32:49.008 --> 32:49.842
Okay, bye.

33:09.946 --> 33:11.572
Hello, this is intern Nam Dong-eun.

33:12.615 --> 33:13.449
Sorry?

33:14.200 --> 33:15.994
I am observing the surgery.

33:16.077 --> 33:18.788
Really? Where are you right now?

33:20.373 --> 33:21.541
I'm at OR 2.

33:25.503 --> 33:26.337
Hello?

33:34.012 --> 33:35.221
Dr. Nam.

33:35.304 --> 33:37.849
OR 2 was for Urology.

33:37.932 --> 33:39.267
OB-GYN is OR 10.

33:43.312 --> 33:45.898
I mean, you're supposed
to observe a hysterectomy,

33:46.399 --> 33:48.735
so why observe a prostatectomy?

33:48.818 --> 33:50.403
There's no uterus there.

33:50.486 --> 33:52.196
Gosh, I'm sorry.

33:52.280 --> 33:53.281
Hey, Dr. Nam.

33:58.786 --> 34:00.288
It can happen.

34:01.956 --> 34:04.459
ORs are chaotic and nerve-wracking.

34:04.542 --> 34:07.545
You can get the people and rooms mixed up.

34:08.629 --> 34:11.090
I'll be more careful from now on.

34:13.051 --> 34:15.303
I told Dr. Ku

34:15.386 --> 34:17.680
you received a call
for an EKG in the ward.

34:19.015 --> 34:20.308
So tell him that if he asks.

34:20.892 --> 34:23.311
Okay. Thank you.

34:25.980 --> 34:30.276
But have you always been bad with numbers?

34:32.195 --> 34:34.155
I was good at math,

34:35.239 --> 34:36.616
so I'm not sure why I'm like this.

34:40.912 --> 34:43.664
She forgets to do her own work,
but gets on my case to do better.

34:43.748 --> 34:45.750
It's better than badgering
while slacking off.

34:45.833 --> 34:47.376
If I ask, she says, "Ask later."

34:47.460 --> 34:49.170
If I do, she says, "Why don't you know?"

34:49.253 --> 34:51.214
It's better than "Do it again"
without checking!

34:51.297 --> 34:52.507
Again, again!

34:52.590 --> 34:53.716
Hey, be quiet!

34:53.800 --> 34:55.134
-I'm upset!
-I'm upset!

34:56.719 --> 34:59.388
Since when did you two get along so well?

34:59.972 --> 35:01.849
Yeah, stop bad-mouthing them.

35:01.933 --> 35:04.602
And it's not hard only for you.
It's hard for our seniors too.

35:05.645 --> 35:08.981
After mentoring the intern,
I realized how hard it was.

35:09.774 --> 35:12.693
It must have been a pain
for them to mold us into decent doctors.

35:13.903 --> 35:16.989
That's still an ongoing process, okay?

35:22.078 --> 35:24.580
For crying out loud.
Can we get some work done?

35:24.664 --> 35:25.540
Sorry.

35:27.542 --> 35:29.127
Use scratch paper for scribbling.

35:29.794 --> 35:31.963
Hey, this isn't scribbling.

35:32.046 --> 35:33.840
Someone asked for my autograph.

35:33.923 --> 35:34.882
Yeah, right.

35:36.300 --> 35:38.761
Hey. Sa-bi, you saw it.

35:38.845 --> 35:40.179
You were there.

35:40.263 --> 35:41.722
Hey, tell her!

35:41.806 --> 35:43.933
Room 1020's guardian is a Hello Girl.

35:44.016 --> 35:45.977
A Hello Girl? What's that?

35:46.060 --> 35:47.353
That's the name of his fan club.

35:48.146 --> 35:50.189
From our hit songs
to the variety shows we were on,

35:50.273 --> 35:52.358
she knows all of our history.

35:52.441 --> 35:55.111
She cried more when we broke up
than for her mother's surgery.

35:55.194 --> 35:58.030
I don't care if it's HI-BOYZ or BYE-BOYZ,

35:58.698 --> 36:01.993
but if you're not going to quit,
you should start doing some work.

36:03.995 --> 36:06.247
TO PARK YU-HYEON
HELLO GIRL! FOREVER! THANK YOU

36:06.831 --> 36:08.791
I will after my meet-and-greet.

36:11.210 --> 36:12.128
Want to come too?

36:14.088 --> 36:15.131
No, right?

36:15.798 --> 36:16.632
See you tomorrow.

36:21.929 --> 36:22.805
Hello?

36:23.806 --> 36:25.308
Yes, I'm on call tonight.

36:27.143 --> 36:28.352
I'll go check now!

36:29.770 --> 36:31.647
I heard she was bleeding and checked.

36:31.731 --> 36:34.400
It's continued,
and pulse is up from two hours ago,

36:34.483 --> 36:35.401
so I called you.

36:37.778 --> 36:40.114
Yes, we'll keep an eye on this for now.

36:40.198 --> 36:42.658
What? But she's bleeding a lot.

36:45.119 --> 36:45.953
Ma'am.

36:46.537 --> 36:50.541
Sometimes, there can be some bleeding
from the surgical site.

36:51.375 --> 36:52.376
Really?

36:53.502 --> 36:55.838
I don't have to do
the surgery again, right?

36:56.672 --> 36:59.842
Maybe if there's more bleeding,
but it's still okay right now.

37:01.427 --> 37:03.721
Let's keep an eye on it until the morning.

37:04.305 --> 37:05.181
Okay.

37:12.480 --> 37:15.399
Doctor, it's not active bleeding, right?

37:15.900 --> 37:17.318
Does she need embolization?

37:17.860 --> 37:21.906
The pad count's low,
and the bleeding's just mild and oozing.

37:21.989 --> 37:23.449
We can monitor her for now.

37:24.116 --> 37:27.453
We need to check her hemoglobin,
so do a lab test for that.

37:27.536 --> 37:28.371
Okay.

37:39.715 --> 37:45.012
ACTIVE BLEEDING
ONGOING FROM THE STUMP AT 6 O'CLOCK

37:59.527 --> 38:00.653
Hello, this is Kim Sa-bi.

38:00.736 --> 38:03.447
Doctor, it's about Ms. Yoo San-ho,
who you checked at 2:00 a.m.

38:03.531 --> 38:05.116
Yes. What is it?

38:05.783 --> 38:09.537
Judging from the continued bleeding,
I think it's active bleeding.

38:09.620 --> 38:11.122
I said it wasn't.

38:11.205 --> 38:13.916
The bleeding's minimal but persistent.

38:14.000 --> 38:16.127
And her hemoglobin's dropped to the tens.

38:16.210 --> 38:19.964
I followed up and BP's 100 over 70,
pulse is 105, pad count is 200.

38:20.047 --> 38:22.216
I checked everything too.

38:22.883 --> 38:24.010
She's fine.

38:38.941 --> 38:42.111
6:00 A.M. PAD COUNT

39:25.529 --> 39:26.947
Hello, this is Kim Sa-bi.

39:28.699 --> 39:29.700
Professor.

39:30.951 --> 39:33.204
It's about Ms. Yoo San-ho
who had a hysterectomy today.

39:33.287 --> 39:35.664
She's had vaginal bleeding since midnight.

39:36.290 --> 39:39.168
It appears to be active bleeding.

39:42.546 --> 39:43.381
Hey, Kim Sa-bi!

39:44.799 --> 39:48.135
Repeat what you said to me
when you called at 2:58 a.m.

39:48.719 --> 39:51.722
Ms. Yoo San-ho.
BP is 100 over 70. Pulse is 105.

39:52.306 --> 39:53.599
Pad count is 200.

39:54.183 --> 39:56.310
And hemoglobin is in the tens.

39:57.561 --> 39:59.438
-Cha Da-hye.
-Yes, sir?

39:59.522 --> 40:01.273
What should we do in this case?

40:02.233 --> 40:04.652
Closely monitor her until morning.

40:04.735 --> 40:06.237
If there are no abnormalities,

40:06.320 --> 40:08.656
we should notify you
during morning rounds.

40:11.784 --> 40:12.660
Right?

40:14.745 --> 40:16.288
-Cha Da-hye.
-Yes, sir?

40:16.372 --> 40:20.251
Why be on call
if you're not going to help? Why?

40:21.460 --> 40:24.255
A first-year calling a professor
directly is ridiculous.

40:24.338 --> 40:26.674
Then why have seniority
or senior doctors at all?

40:28.676 --> 40:29.677
I'm sorry, sir.

40:31.137 --> 40:33.305
Between the first-year
who calls about such things

40:33.806 --> 40:35.933
and the second-year
who doesn't check them,

40:37.351 --> 40:39.103
you two are a complete mess.

40:43.607 --> 40:44.608
You two

40:45.401 --> 40:48.320
better not continue
to work so cluelessly like this.

40:57.496 --> 40:59.248
I'm sorry, Dr. Cha.

41:00.291 --> 41:02.293
The thing is, I thought…

41:08.674 --> 41:10.801
Hey, Sa-bi. Want to eat?

41:28.777 --> 41:30.488
It's today, isn't it? Right?

41:34.116 --> 41:35.451
If something happens by chance--

41:35.534 --> 41:37.870
Don't say that. That's inviting bad luck.

41:48.297 --> 41:49.131
See you later.

41:56.597 --> 41:58.974
Doctor, I think it's started.

41:59.058 --> 42:00.017
Right.

42:03.896 --> 42:05.481
We'll have her begin pushing.

42:08.484 --> 42:10.486
Ma'am, we're going to start pushing now.

42:10.569 --> 42:12.029
Watch me and follow along.

42:12.112 --> 42:13.072
Okay.

42:14.114 --> 42:15.449
Where's Dr. Myeong?

42:15.533 --> 42:16.534
She's with an outpatient.

42:16.617 --> 42:17.993
You can push with me,

42:18.077 --> 42:20.496
and when we're ready for delivery,
she'll come.

42:20.579 --> 42:21.455
Okay.

42:21.539 --> 42:22.873
-Let's get in position.
-Okay.

42:25.334 --> 42:27.795
Pull below your thighs and hold them.

42:27.878 --> 42:29.088
One, two, three.

42:29.755 --> 42:30.589
Push.

42:30.673 --> 42:34.218
More, more! As long as you can!

42:35.386 --> 42:37.346
Take a breath, and again.

42:37.429 --> 42:39.014
Push harder. We have a ways to go.

42:41.892 --> 42:44.061
Okay, one, two, three. Push!

42:46.272 --> 42:47.314
Push!

42:47.398 --> 42:49.775
A bit more!

42:49.858 --> 42:51.443
Ma'am, you have to keep it together.

42:51.527 --> 42:53.112
If you don't push, the baby won't come.

42:53.195 --> 42:55.656
The baby's done all it can.
You just need to push.

42:57.908 --> 42:59.743
Doctor, there's too little progress.

42:59.827 --> 43:01.412
It's been almost two hours.

43:01.495 --> 43:02.663
Damn it, what could be wrong?

43:06.458 --> 43:07.668
MYEONG EUN-WON

43:14.800 --> 43:17.553
DOCTOR, WE'VE BEEN PUSHING FOR TWO HOURS.
THERE'S NO CHANGE. SHOULD WE PREP THE OR?

43:17.636 --> 43:18.929
Why isn't she replying after reading?

43:22.016 --> 43:23.434
Ma'am, are you really tired?

43:26.812 --> 43:29.023
-Let's try another ultrasound.
-Okay.

43:42.911 --> 43:44.288
I made eye contact with the baby.

43:44.371 --> 43:45.748
You can see its eyes.

43:50.961 --> 43:53.380
It's easier to deliver
when the baby's face-down,

43:53.464 --> 43:55.257
but it's face-up,
so you're finding it hard.

43:57.801 --> 43:59.678
Then what do we do?

44:00.888 --> 44:01.722
Well…

44:02.806 --> 44:05.768
You're going to have to
push more and much harder.

44:05.851 --> 44:06.810
Let's try it.

44:06.894 --> 44:08.562
Okay, push harder. Again.

44:09.396 --> 44:11.315
One, two, three, and inhale!

44:13.484 --> 44:14.318
Push!

44:15.778 --> 44:18.113
Harder! Longer!

44:18.197 --> 44:19.073
More!

44:23.202 --> 44:24.078
Just a second.

44:27.331 --> 44:28.374
Yes, Doctor?

44:28.457 --> 44:30.501
Doctor, it's about Ms. Yong Jin-suk.

44:30.584 --> 44:32.670
Did you check
the chest X-ray interpretation?

44:34.505 --> 44:36.632
I did put in a request earlier,

44:36.715 --> 44:38.801
but I haven't checked yet.

44:39.510 --> 44:40.594
I'm sorry.

44:40.678 --> 44:43.263
Then what about
the OTPT follow-up results?

44:44.223 --> 44:45.474
Just a moment.

44:45.557 --> 44:47.017
Let me check.

44:56.527 --> 44:57.986
When I saw it earlier,

44:58.070 --> 45:00.656
I don't think the results were in.

45:01.573 --> 45:02.866
What about the hemoglobin level?

45:04.034 --> 45:06.120
I'm not sure about that either…

45:07.037 --> 45:08.163
I see.

45:09.123 --> 45:10.874
I'll go to the ward later
and check myself.

45:11.417 --> 45:12.251
It's okay.

45:12.835 --> 45:14.128
Thank you, Doctor.

45:15.421 --> 45:16.505
I'm sorry.

45:19.550 --> 45:21.260
-Shouldn't you go?
-No.

45:22.010 --> 45:22.845
It's okay.

45:24.221 --> 45:26.265
You didn't know anything.
Won't you get in trouble?

45:28.142 --> 45:30.686
Nope. He's a first-year resident.

45:30.769 --> 45:31.895
He's super nice.

45:31.979 --> 45:34.356
He never gets mad or annoyed.

45:34.440 --> 45:35.774
He doesn't even scold me.

45:37.276 --> 45:38.485
You're so lucky.

45:39.486 --> 45:40.446
Should I choose OB-GYN?

45:42.030 --> 45:44.491
If I don't do my work, he does it for me.

45:44.575 --> 45:47.911
He covers up my mistakes
and does anything I ask for.

45:49.163 --> 45:51.081
He's a bit of a… How do I put it?

45:51.999 --> 45:53.500
He's kind of a pushover.

45:53.584 --> 45:54.751
Damn.

45:56.336 --> 45:59.423
I can just wing it, and he does the rest.

46:06.472 --> 46:07.848
Your name was Nam Dong-eun?

46:11.435 --> 46:12.436
Enjoy your food.

46:44.259 --> 46:45.344
Dr. Nam.

46:45.427 --> 46:46.929
Ms. Baek Geum-yeong's ABGA.

46:48.138 --> 46:49.932
I was going to do it now. I swear.

46:50.015 --> 46:51.099
I did it.

46:51.683 --> 46:52.893
You seemed busy earlier.

46:57.022 --> 46:58.023
Thank you.

47:03.403 --> 47:04.404
And…

47:06.865 --> 47:08.116
I'm sorry.

47:11.620 --> 47:12.621
It's fine.

47:13.205 --> 47:16.041
When you're an intern,
ABGA is the hardest to do.

47:17.167 --> 47:18.919
And your hands shake
if they start to hurt.

47:19.503 --> 47:22.756
No, it's not that. Earlier--

47:22.839 --> 47:24.174
By October of your first year,

47:24.258 --> 47:25.634
you just toss the syringe,

47:26.385 --> 47:28.637
and it lands perfectly in their wrist.

47:30.013 --> 47:30.847
Doctor.

47:30.931 --> 47:31.765
That was a joke.

47:35.352 --> 47:38.105
You can go home now.
I don't have any more tasks for you.

47:43.735 --> 47:45.195
It's all right.

47:46.446 --> 47:47.406
You can go.

47:52.369 --> 47:53.245
Okay.

48:00.210 --> 48:01.086
Good night, sir.

48:09.136 --> 48:10.095
I'm sorry.

48:12.014 --> 48:12.889
See you tomorrow.

48:22.149 --> 48:24.901
Jae-il, Ms. Yoon Su-mi's
blood test results…

48:30.073 --> 48:30.991
Doctor.

48:49.092 --> 48:50.761
You don't even smoke. Why come here?

48:52.471 --> 48:55.140
They say if you smoke
when you're frustrated, you feel better.

48:56.558 --> 48:58.435
I wanted to imagine what it was like.

49:02.773 --> 49:03.857
What do you want me to do?

49:04.483 --> 49:05.317
What?

49:05.400 --> 49:08.070
That bastard.
You want me to go yell at him?

49:08.153 --> 49:10.739
Or drag him here to make him apologize?

49:12.240 --> 49:13.492
You're not going to do that.

49:17.746 --> 49:18.622
I mean…

49:20.040 --> 49:22.417
I just don't think
it's my place to interfere.

49:25.420 --> 49:26.296
Right.

49:28.048 --> 49:29.132
It's my problem to solve.

49:32.844 --> 49:33.679
Um Jae-il.

49:35.263 --> 49:37.974
Getting mad
and scolding someone isn't easy.

49:38.058 --> 49:41.603
The one scolding feels uncomfortable,
self-conscious, and unpleasant.

49:41.687 --> 49:43.647
But you still have to do it.

49:43.730 --> 49:46.983
We do it for a reason.
If you make a mistake, you'll be scolded.

49:47.067 --> 49:48.068
And for interns,

49:48.151 --> 49:51.154
they need someone who scolds them
to teach them what's right

49:51.238 --> 49:52.656
rather than a nice person.

49:54.491 --> 49:55.492
I don't think so.

49:56.576 --> 49:59.579
Instead of being scary and scolding,
when they said, "It's okay,"

49:59.663 --> 50:01.164
"You can do better next time,"

50:01.248 --> 50:03.709
"It was our mistake, not yours,"

50:03.792 --> 50:07.546
it made me want to do better
and never make a mistake again.

50:07.629 --> 50:08.630
Who did that?

50:08.714 --> 50:09.631
Dr. Ki Eun-mi.

50:11.341 --> 50:12.426
Hey, that's…

50:15.387 --> 50:17.013
That's because you're nice.

50:18.473 --> 50:21.393
Since you're nice,
you accept her kindness with thanks.

50:21.476 --> 50:22.436
That's who you are.

50:22.519 --> 50:23.729
That's why that worked on you.

50:23.812 --> 50:27.232
There aren't many people like that
in the world or even here.

50:27.315 --> 50:29.317
Most would take advantage of
and belittle you.

50:30.861 --> 50:34.656
Life's easy when you're mean.
Who'd live foolishly like you guys?

50:35.907 --> 50:38.493
What do I do now then?

50:41.329 --> 50:43.248
I can't tell you to be mean though.

50:45.500 --> 50:46.710
Gosh, I don't know.

50:49.963 --> 50:52.758
Scold mistakes and praise success.
Start with that.

50:52.841 --> 50:55.886
Then don't you think
you'll develop a sense

50:56.762 --> 50:59.222
of when to get mad and when to comfort?

51:00.640 --> 51:01.475
Right.

51:02.434 --> 51:05.812
If you're just clear about that,
the juniors seemed to appreciate it.

51:07.022 --> 51:07.856
Okay.

51:10.817 --> 51:11.735
But, Doctor…

51:13.945 --> 51:15.947
have I ever told you I loved you?

51:16.031 --> 51:17.157
And very much at that.

51:18.867 --> 51:19.701
Bye.

51:25.081 --> 51:25.999
Wait for me!

51:30.212 --> 51:32.589
Ma'am, you have to breathe
to get oxygen to the baby.

51:32.672 --> 51:35.634
Inhale deeply and exhale.

51:35.717 --> 51:37.135
Very good.

51:37.219 --> 51:39.137
Breathe in and exhale.

51:39.221 --> 51:41.139
Doctor, did you get my text?

51:41.640 --> 51:42.849
I don't think a VD will work.

51:42.933 --> 51:44.309
Try for another 30 minutes.

51:44.392 --> 51:46.520
No, we can't. We really can't now.

51:46.603 --> 51:48.605
I told you the baby's OP.

51:48.688 --> 51:50.148
The baby's not coming at all.

51:50.232 --> 51:51.942
Did you do things properly?

51:52.025 --> 51:53.693
Yes, we've worked really hard.

51:53.777 --> 51:55.487
And she's still pushing now.

51:55.570 --> 51:57.781
It's been almost three hours
and it's still in station.

51:57.864 --> 51:58.865
The fetus is OP too.

51:58.949 --> 52:01.451
The mother's too exhausted to go on.

52:01.535 --> 52:02.619
So?

52:02.702 --> 52:05.914
She's been pushing for almost three hours,
and you want surgery now?

52:05.997 --> 52:07.707
Yes, that's what I'm saying.

52:08.208 --> 52:09.292
Should I book an OR?

52:12.212 --> 52:13.338
Doctor?

52:13.421 --> 52:16.049
Hey, are you telling me
to do a full C-section?

52:16.132 --> 52:17.801
Don't you know that's the worst?

52:17.884 --> 52:18.927
I know.

52:20.804 --> 52:22.097
But I think we need to.

52:22.681 --> 52:25.767
I said I promised her a VD.
How many times have I told you?

52:26.393 --> 52:29.229
No! We have to do surgery!

52:29.312 --> 52:32.190
Hey, are you out of your mind?
How dare you use informal--

52:36.236 --> 52:38.655
Hold your breath a bit more.
Just once more!

52:38.738 --> 52:40.323
Are you okay, Ms. Song?

52:40.407 --> 52:41.491
Let me take a look.

52:41.992 --> 52:44.661
Doctor, it hurts so much!

52:46.329 --> 52:49.165
She can't push and has been in labor
for almost three hours.

52:49.249 --> 52:50.250
They said an OR is open.

52:55.213 --> 52:57.257
She's having a really hard time,
and if the baby…

52:58.466 --> 52:59.467
If deceleration worsens…

53:07.392 --> 53:08.226
Dr. Oh!

53:11.771 --> 53:13.565
Why haven't you booked an OR yet?

53:14.149 --> 53:16.234
Were you waiting
until the fetal monitor signs dropped?

53:16.902 --> 53:18.069
Is your judgement that poor?

53:18.820 --> 53:19.738
I've been saying--

53:19.821 --> 53:22.324
What are you doing?
Get her to the OR! Now!

53:46.681 --> 53:49.100
I LIKE YOU A LOT TOO

53:54.022 --> 53:56.983
-Hello?
-Hello, I'm the flower courier.

53:57.067 --> 53:59.361
Instead of the lobby,
please come to the parking lot.

53:59.444 --> 54:01.196
Come all the way in, please.

54:01.279 --> 54:02.364
Well, the thing is…

54:02.864 --> 54:03.990
I'm sorry.

54:04.741 --> 54:05.617
What?

54:07.327 --> 54:08.453
Were you the one who called?

54:09.496 --> 54:11.247
-Are you Ku Do-won?
-Yes.

54:12.082 --> 54:12.916
I'm sorry.

54:13.500 --> 54:15.502
I ran into a bus out front.

54:15.585 --> 54:16.503
So they're…

54:18.046 --> 54:18.880
No, it's okay.

54:19.422 --> 54:21.508
Are you all right?
Were you hurt anywhere else?

54:21.591 --> 54:23.593
No, I'm fine.

54:23.677 --> 54:24.928
But the flowers are…

54:25.512 --> 54:26.346
I'm sorry.

54:26.930 --> 54:28.515
It's all right. Don't worry about it.

54:29.099 --> 54:29.975
I'm sorry.

54:32.310 --> 54:33.687
-Mr. Park Jeong-woong?
-Yes?

54:34.688 --> 54:36.356
-Do you feel any pain anywhere else?
-No.

54:36.439 --> 54:37.399
Hello?

54:37.482 --> 54:39.401
This is Bon Moment.

54:39.484 --> 54:40.318
Yes?

54:40.402 --> 54:42.278
I'd like to confirm your reservation.

54:42.362 --> 54:44.030
For two at 9:00 p.m. tomorrow…

54:44.114 --> 54:45.198
No, it's today.

54:45.281 --> 54:47.826
Sorry? You reserved it for tomorrow.

54:48.535 --> 54:50.036
I reserved for the 13th.

54:50.120 --> 54:53.456
Yes, that's tomorrow. Today's the 12th.

54:55.083 --> 54:56.042
Damn it.

54:59.295 --> 55:00.380
I'm sorry.

55:00.463 --> 55:02.590
I'm sorry, but are there any tables today?

55:03.675 --> 55:05.635
We're fully booked today.

55:09.305 --> 55:12.100
I'm sorry, I can't do tomorrow,
so I'll have to cancel.

55:12.934 --> 55:15.228
Pull. More!

55:18.523 --> 55:19.649
Remove the instrument.

55:23.653 --> 55:24.487
Fundal.

55:30.827 --> 55:31.828
The baby's out.

55:32.412 --> 55:34.664
It's 7:35 p.m., and it's a boy.

55:35.373 --> 55:37.792
He's healthy and so beautiful.

55:37.876 --> 55:39.377
You can see him soon.

55:39.461 --> 55:41.171
Thank you.

55:45.383 --> 55:47.469
We'll remove the placenta
and start suturing now.

55:47.552 --> 55:49.846
You may feel some discomfort.

55:59.856 --> 56:03.318
CENTRAL OPERATING UNIT

56:03.401 --> 56:05.028
Nice work, Dr. Oh.

56:05.653 --> 56:06.946
You did great,

56:07.739 --> 56:11.326
but you'll need to study more
on dystocia criteria and section timing.

56:12.077 --> 56:14.537
It's okay.
You can ask me questions anytime.

56:21.503 --> 56:24.130
Mr. Jang, we got it.

56:24.214 --> 56:26.841
Thrills, touching moments,
and quotable lines. It has it all.

56:27.509 --> 56:28.968
I think this will be a hit.

56:36.476 --> 56:37.936
SECOND-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE
OB-GYN

56:50.281 --> 56:51.449
Who is it?

56:52.075 --> 56:54.035
It's Kim Sa-bi.

57:04.254 --> 57:05.088
I'm sorry.

57:07.841 --> 57:10.718
I was wrong. I made a mistake.

57:12.387 --> 57:13.263
It's fine.

57:14.097 --> 57:15.723
I already got yelled at anyways.

57:16.307 --> 57:17.267
What else can I do?

57:21.729 --> 57:24.607
If you're not going to listen to me
and do your own thing,

57:24.691 --> 57:26.401
why bother updating me?

57:27.026 --> 57:29.154
Why? Just do things on your own now.

57:29.237 --> 57:30.405
You're smart.

57:31.906 --> 57:32.907
I'm sorry.

57:33.825 --> 57:36.661
It's all my fault,
so I don't know what to say.

57:39.831 --> 57:42.625
So instead of just verbally apologizing,

57:44.043 --> 57:46.713
I thought about
what I should do going forward.

57:50.383 --> 57:53.928
From now on, I won't mess around
and solely trust my own judgement.

57:56.473 --> 58:00.852
So to do that, until all my suspicions
and curiosities go away,

58:02.437 --> 58:04.022
I'm going to ask you everything.

58:05.565 --> 58:08.443
Until I'm absolutely sure
and have no more questions left--

58:08.526 --> 58:09.444
Don't.

58:09.527 --> 58:10.737
What?

58:10.820 --> 58:11.905
I said don't.

58:11.988 --> 58:13.990
Don't ask me questions!

58:14.073 --> 58:16.534
I don't know either! Okay?

58:16.618 --> 58:19.954
We're all in the same boat!
We're both idiots!

58:20.038 --> 58:23.625
How can a second-year admit
to a first-year that they don't know?

58:23.708 --> 58:24.751
That's embarrassing!

58:26.711 --> 58:28.505
Damn it, this is so embarrassing.

58:34.677 --> 58:36.971
But not knowing
is nothing to be ashamed of.

58:38.139 --> 58:38.973
What?

58:39.974 --> 58:40.808
I'm sorry.

58:41.601 --> 58:44.020
Damn it, Sa-bi.

58:44.812 --> 58:45.897
But, Dr. Cha…

58:46.689 --> 58:47.524
Well,

58:48.358 --> 58:51.152
there's nothing
I'm curious about in that book.

58:51.736 --> 58:54.030
I know everything in it.

58:57.075 --> 58:59.160
Well, good for you.

58:59.244 --> 59:00.703
How very nice!

59:01.704 --> 59:02.914
I'm sorry.

59:04.499 --> 59:05.500
Don't smile.

59:07.126 --> 59:08.294
I'm still angry!

59:11.172 --> 59:12.006
Don't smirk!

59:12.840 --> 59:14.050
I said I'm still mad!

59:24.852 --> 59:25.853
Ta-da.

59:27.146 --> 59:29.482
I really needed this right now.
How'd you know?

59:30.441 --> 59:31.609
Because we're a team.

59:37.991 --> 59:40.702
I told Nam Dong-eun
to finish the dressings before leaving.

59:40.785 --> 59:43.246
He tried his best.
But he can't help being slow.

59:43.913 --> 59:45.540
After I finish this, I'll do it.

59:45.623 --> 59:47.458
Damn it.

59:47.542 --> 59:50.628
Hey, you were the same.
You don't remember, do you?

59:50.712 --> 59:53.047
Doctor, how can you smile right now?

59:53.131 --> 59:55.258
Then should I cry
that he didn't do the dressings?

01:00:03.057 --> 01:00:04.517
I'll start with Room 1011.

01:00:04.601 --> 01:00:05.643
Forget it. Go home.

01:00:06.352 --> 01:00:07.353
You go home instead.

01:00:07.437 --> 01:00:08.688
I can do it.

01:00:08.771 --> 01:00:10.773
No, I can do it. I'm doing it.

01:01:26.891 --> 01:01:28.393
Why is there so much to write?

01:01:32.188 --> 01:01:33.898
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

01:01:35.900 --> 01:01:37.193
I, Oh Yi-young,

01:01:37.902 --> 01:01:41.114
can no longer stand
Dr. Myeong Eun-won's tyranny.

01:01:41.197 --> 01:01:43.908
It's become too hard
to hold back my pent-up anger,

01:01:44.575 --> 01:01:46.285
which is why I am resigning.

01:01:50.790 --> 01:01:51.708
PRINT

01:01:57.880 --> 01:01:59.006
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

01:02:05.471 --> 01:02:06.597
Hey!

01:02:11.769 --> 01:02:12.645
Here.

01:02:13.980 --> 01:02:15.565
I don't give these to anyone.

01:02:15.648 --> 01:02:16.649
It's nonalcoholic.

01:02:28.619 --> 01:02:29.746
Dr. Myeong?

01:02:31.247 --> 01:02:32.457
Why does she only pick on me?

01:02:33.040 --> 01:02:36.461
You were in her doghouse in March.
Did something happen after that?

01:02:37.378 --> 01:02:39.005
I stood up to her once.

01:02:39.756 --> 01:02:40.673
Or did I confront her?

01:02:42.717 --> 01:02:45.636
In any case, we just don't get along.

01:02:45.720 --> 01:02:48.055
She's… weird.

01:02:48.139 --> 01:02:49.307
She has no damn shame.

01:02:50.183 --> 01:02:52.518
I thought I was watching a one-woman show.

01:02:52.602 --> 01:02:54.562
When I was texting
and calling her for surgery,

01:02:54.645 --> 01:02:55.897
she went on and on about a VD.

01:02:55.980 --> 01:02:56.898
Then all of a sudden,

01:02:56.981 --> 01:02:59.025
"What are you doing? Get an OR!"

01:03:01.527 --> 01:03:04.280
She glared at me all through the surgery.

01:03:04.363 --> 01:03:05.323
But with the camera on,

01:03:06.741 --> 01:03:08.451
"Ask me anything if you have questions."

01:03:10.119 --> 01:03:12.622
Like that. Gosh, she thinks
she's some master surgeon.

01:03:13.581 --> 01:03:15.082
I was sure this was nonalcoholic.

01:03:16.083 --> 01:03:17.001
I can't do it anymore.

01:03:17.084 --> 01:03:18.085
I won't take it.

01:03:20.338 --> 01:03:21.672
You're really quitting?

01:03:22.215 --> 01:03:23.049
Yeah.

01:03:23.132 --> 01:03:25.259
I'm leaving before I cause trouble again.

01:03:25.343 --> 01:03:26.177
Trouble?

01:03:27.595 --> 01:03:29.764
Hey, those rumors were true?

01:03:29.847 --> 01:03:31.098
At the local hospital?

01:03:35.895 --> 01:03:38.815
You sure are incredible.

01:03:42.777 --> 01:03:43.903
But isn't it such a waste?

01:03:44.529 --> 01:03:47.406
You've made it to October
enduring this mean and nasty first year.

01:03:47.490 --> 01:03:48.866
I won't come back anyways.

01:03:49.450 --> 01:03:50.368
I don't need this.

01:03:50.451 --> 01:03:51.327
Really?

01:03:52.620 --> 01:03:54.330
Then I guess you don't need that either.

01:03:58.042 --> 01:04:00.545
The end-of-year bonus.
We get it in December.

01:04:02.129 --> 01:04:03.464
You just need to wait two months.

01:04:04.340 --> 01:04:05.758
That's too bad.

01:04:09.011 --> 01:04:09.887
How much is it?

01:04:10.847 --> 01:04:11.722
Quite a bit.

01:04:16.686 --> 01:04:18.771
Why do they give bonuses in December?

01:04:19.772 --> 01:04:21.357
That's so annoying!

01:04:24.110 --> 01:04:25.444
KU DO-WON

01:04:30.825 --> 01:04:31.951
Yes, Doctor?

01:04:33.202 --> 01:04:34.287
I'm sorry.

01:04:35.538 --> 01:04:37.540
But could we reschedule our plans?

01:04:37.623 --> 01:04:38.958
Why?

01:04:40.334 --> 01:04:43.212
I'm sorry. Something came up.

01:04:46.799 --> 01:04:47.842
Fine.

01:04:49.051 --> 01:04:50.052
Okay, bye.

01:04:51.762 --> 01:04:52.805
What was that?

01:04:52.889 --> 01:04:54.849
How come nothing ever goes my way?

01:04:55.766 --> 01:04:57.101
I told you.

01:04:58.060 --> 01:04:59.228
"A week of war."

01:05:01.439 --> 01:05:03.190
I told you it's really accurate.

01:05:14.160 --> 01:05:17.413
In any case, don't read me
my fortune anymore.

01:05:17.496 --> 01:05:20.917
Me too. It's better not to know.
There's no solution anyway.

01:05:21.542 --> 01:05:24.253
Hey, we can't go on like this.
Let's go change our luck.

01:05:24.837 --> 01:05:26.047
I checked our horoscopes today.

01:05:26.130 --> 01:05:28.299
-Don't.
-What is it? What did it say?

01:05:29.008 --> 01:05:31.427
Sa-bi's lucky number is 12.

01:05:31.510 --> 01:05:33.721
Yi-young's lucky drink is beer.

01:05:33.804 --> 01:05:35.056
Nam-kyung's lucky place?

01:05:35.139 --> 01:05:36.057
Karaoke.

01:05:36.140 --> 01:05:38.476
-What? You saw it too?
-Yeah.

01:05:38.559 --> 01:05:39.894
Okay, but listen.

01:05:39.977 --> 01:05:41.896
Today's the 12th.

01:05:42.480 --> 01:05:44.607
And none of us are on call.

01:05:44.690 --> 01:05:45.983
So we can drink beer.

01:05:46.567 --> 01:05:47.944
And where do we go after drinking?

01:05:48.694 --> 01:05:49.612
Karaoke!

01:05:49.695 --> 01:05:52.365
It sounds like you made up
those connections just to hang out.

01:05:52.448 --> 01:05:53.532
No.

01:05:53.616 --> 01:05:55.910
Our horoscopes are telling us to have fun!

01:05:55.993 --> 01:05:58.120
Hey. Let's go. Come on.

01:05:58.704 --> 01:06:00.081
Let's have fun for just one night!

01:06:01.290 --> 01:06:02.375
She won't go though.

01:06:04.835 --> 01:06:05.670
Let's go.

01:06:06.545 --> 01:06:08.422
What? What's gotten into you?

01:06:08.506 --> 01:06:09.632
Today, I…

01:06:12.843 --> 01:06:14.053
Whatever. Let's drink.

01:06:14.136 --> 01:06:15.805
You're serious, right? Then…

01:06:17.139 --> 01:06:19.100
We need raw eggs for karaoke.

01:06:19.934 --> 01:06:21.310
You carry raw eggs around?

01:06:21.894 --> 01:06:23.062
You never know when you'll go.

01:06:23.145 --> 01:06:24.313
Got anything else?

01:06:24.397 --> 01:06:25.982
Like anti-hangover drinks?

01:06:28.234 --> 01:06:29.527
Ta-da!

01:06:30.361 --> 01:06:31.737
Here, take one each.

01:06:33.030 --> 01:06:34.407
You're the best, Jae-il.

01:06:35.157 --> 01:06:36.242
What else is in there?

01:06:36.325 --> 01:06:38.119
I knew this day would come.

01:06:38.202 --> 01:06:40.621
Okay. Bottoms up, everyone.

01:06:40.705 --> 01:06:42.248
-Bottoms up!
-Bottoms up!

01:06:47.712 --> 01:06:49.505
Hey, let's go. We can't waste a minute.

01:06:51.549 --> 01:06:55.344
We should have been friends

01:06:55.428 --> 01:06:58.264
And let everything go

01:06:59.181 --> 01:07:00.725
Seeing you with someone else…

01:07:00.808 --> 01:07:03.602
Hey, you're really not singing?
There are only three minutes left.

01:07:04.186 --> 01:07:05.479
No, I'm not in the mood.

01:07:07.732 --> 01:07:08.816
You're not singing either?

01:07:11.027 --> 01:07:11.986
You're going to sing?

01:07:13.070 --> 01:07:14.447
I need to go to the restroom.

01:07:14.530 --> 01:07:16.449
Then I'll do a song. Okay?

01:07:17.033 --> 01:07:18.826
At least listen to the last song first.

01:07:18.909 --> 01:07:22.079
To see you a bit longer

01:07:22.163 --> 01:07:25.291
If I see you again--

01:07:26.167 --> 01:07:27.084
Hey!

01:07:27.168 --> 01:07:29.086
I was just at the climax of the song!

01:07:29.170 --> 01:07:30.796
Goodness, I'm sorry.

01:07:30.880 --> 01:07:32.048
You did that on purpose.

01:07:32.131 --> 01:07:33.799
Since you came to karaoke with me,

01:07:33.883 --> 01:07:35.718
you have to hear this before going.

01:07:39.221 --> 01:07:43.559
I pray it's not the end

01:07:43.642 --> 01:07:46.687
I want to hold onto this night

01:07:46.771 --> 01:07:50.107
I can't let you go like this

01:07:51.192 --> 01:07:54.445
Nothing can come between us

01:07:58.908 --> 01:08:00.076
I'm blinded by love…

01:08:00.159 --> 01:08:01.702
He came here to do this.

01:08:02.453 --> 01:08:03.454
Is this the song?

01:08:04.413 --> 01:08:05.498
Yeah, HI-BOYZ.

01:08:05.581 --> 01:08:07.333
And made you cry a lot

01:08:07.416 --> 01:08:10.544
I can't help but love you

01:08:12.004 --> 01:08:14.632
We were both so young

01:08:14.715 --> 01:08:18.844
The foolish memories of my first love

01:08:19.553 --> 01:08:22.139
I hope this song

01:08:22.223 --> 01:08:26.477
Can send us back to those days

01:08:27.770 --> 01:08:31.440
When that day comes, I'll tell you then

01:08:31.524 --> 01:08:33.609
You were my whole life

01:08:34.318 --> 01:08:35.486
Jae-il!

01:08:36.237 --> 01:08:37.363
This is amazing.

01:08:37.446 --> 01:08:39.073
When that day comes

01:08:39.156 --> 01:08:43.160
I'll come running to you

01:08:44.036 --> 01:08:45.079
He's looks so different.

01:08:46.956 --> 01:08:50.292
If that fateful day ever comes

01:08:50.376 --> 01:08:51.293
Why is he so good?

01:08:54.839 --> 01:08:59.593
I hope we can go back to those days

01:08:59.677 --> 01:09:03.514
When that day comes, I'll tell you then

01:09:03.597 --> 01:09:07.476
You were my whole life

01:09:07.560 --> 01:09:09.186
The end of longing

01:09:09.270 --> 01:09:11.188
When that day comes

01:09:11.272 --> 01:09:14.859
I'll come running to you

01:09:18.821 --> 01:09:22.783
If that fateful day ever comes

01:09:26.495 --> 01:09:29.248
I hope we can meet again

01:09:29.331 --> 01:09:31.750
I'll keep wishing on and on

01:09:39.300 --> 01:09:40.342
Holy cow, Sa-bi!

01:09:45.139 --> 01:09:46.056
Did you save that?

01:09:48.851 --> 01:09:50.561
-The K-pop idol!
-Sa-bi, is this right?

01:09:50.644 --> 01:09:51.687
Is it?

01:09:52.354 --> 01:09:54.231
Kim Sa-bi!

01:09:54.315 --> 01:09:55.566
Don't. I said don't!

01:09:56.525 --> 01:09:58.027
So you've always liked them?

01:09:58.110 --> 01:09:58.944
I don't know.

01:10:00.362 --> 01:10:02.406
-Sa-bi. I'm pretty good, right?
-It's here.

01:10:02.489 --> 01:10:03.908
My taxi's here.

01:10:03.991 --> 01:10:05.910
Bye. I want to see an encore next time.

01:10:05.993 --> 01:10:07.119
Bye!

01:10:07.203 --> 01:10:08.495
Once is enough for me.

01:10:08.579 --> 01:10:09.413
See you tomorrow.

01:10:18.714 --> 01:10:20.549
Why is it taking so long?

01:10:23.135 --> 01:10:24.136
What about you?

01:10:24.970 --> 01:10:26.096
I didn't call one yet.

01:10:26.722 --> 01:10:28.140
I wanted to see you all off first.

01:10:35.522 --> 01:10:36.523
Hey.

01:10:37.066 --> 01:10:38.234
Want me to do it for you?

01:10:38.317 --> 01:10:39.443
What?

01:10:42.613 --> 01:10:43.781
Damn it.

01:10:45.324 --> 01:10:47.326
Hey, what's with you?
Why didn't you tell me?

01:10:48.410 --> 01:10:49.245
How did you

01:10:50.120 --> 01:10:51.789
hold in all that excitement during work?

01:10:55.417 --> 01:10:57.503
I'm saying this
to set the record straight.

01:10:58.671 --> 01:10:59.505
I am a fan.

01:11:00.965 --> 01:11:02.091
But not of yours.

01:11:02.758 --> 01:11:03.592
What?

01:11:03.676 --> 01:11:06.679
I liked Top Key, not you.

01:11:07.429 --> 01:11:08.347
Liar.

01:11:08.430 --> 01:11:11.642
And your first music show win
was June 9th, not June 2nd.

01:11:11.725 --> 01:11:13.060
You were a nominee on June 2nd.

01:11:13.644 --> 01:11:16.563
That Hello Girl guardian
had the dates wrong.

01:11:17.398 --> 01:11:18.440
Just so you properly know.

01:11:20.651 --> 01:11:21.485
Okay, then.

01:11:25.447 --> 01:11:26.407
Bye.

01:11:27.366 --> 01:11:28.242
Bye!

01:12:13.662 --> 01:12:15.080
Weren't you supposed to be busy?

01:12:16.040 --> 01:12:16.874
Yes, well…

01:12:19.043 --> 01:12:21.420
You didn't lie to avoid
having dinner with me, did you?

01:12:22.087 --> 01:12:23.589
Why would I lie like that?

01:12:23.672 --> 01:12:25.758
Then why did you cancel on the day of?

01:12:30.054 --> 01:12:31.055
I'm sorry.

01:12:38.103 --> 01:12:41.690
I was so excited
to have dinner with the person I like.

01:12:50.824 --> 01:12:51.950
I'm heading in first.

01:13:00.250 --> 01:13:02.419
To be honest,
tonight's reservation was canceled.

01:13:03.045 --> 01:13:04.213
I bought flowers too, but…

01:13:07.549 --> 01:13:08.550
They got ruined.

01:13:11.303 --> 01:13:12.596
I even wrote you a card.

01:13:20.646 --> 01:13:22.564
I left it there.
I really did write one though.

01:13:26.276 --> 01:13:28.737
So I only have this left.

01:13:33.784 --> 01:13:34.618
I…

01:13:38.997 --> 01:13:39.832
Oh Yi-young…

01:13:45.295 --> 01:13:46.296
I like you…

01:13:49.675 --> 01:13:50.676
You like me?

01:13:51.969 --> 01:13:52.803
Really?

01:13:55.180 --> 01:13:56.765
Are you confessing your feelings to me?

01:13:57.850 --> 01:13:58.684
Yes.

01:14:11.738 --> 01:14:12.781
I…

01:14:15.534 --> 01:14:18.495
I've said how I felt a lot,
so I don't have to tell you, right?

01:14:29.423 --> 01:14:30.257
Then…

01:14:32.926 --> 01:14:33.760
Then…

01:14:40.893 --> 01:14:41.727
We're…

01:15:52.005 --> 01:15:53.966
Let's not tell Joo-young for now.

01:15:55.217 --> 01:15:57.010
I want her IVF to go well first.

01:15:57.844 --> 01:15:58.971
Then I'll tell her.

01:16:00.138 --> 01:16:02.724
You can do whatever you want,
and I'll go along with it.

01:16:31.003 --> 01:16:31.920
That's right.

01:16:35.382 --> 01:16:36.550
Right, they went on a trip.

01:16:38.594 --> 01:16:39.845
They'll be gone for a few days.

01:16:39.928 --> 01:16:41.638
I think they said for four days.

01:16:46.351 --> 01:16:49.146
I have to go to the hospital.
Did I not tell you?

01:16:49.980 --> 01:16:50.814
No.

01:16:51.857 --> 01:16:53.859
So, I have work…

01:16:55.152 --> 01:16:56.903
I mean, I have papers to read.

01:16:58.030 --> 01:16:59.865
-What?
-What?

01:16:59.948 --> 01:17:02.659
I forgot.
I'll sleep at the hospital tonight.

01:17:04.953 --> 01:17:07.581
Are you uncomfortable
with just the two of us here?

01:17:09.833 --> 01:17:12.252
It's been just the two of us
this whole time though.

01:17:17.007 --> 01:17:19.051
I guess being in the house is a bit much.

01:17:28.393 --> 01:17:29.603
Here's okay though?

01:17:51.041 --> 01:17:51.958
Get in.

01:17:52.042 --> 01:17:53.543
I'll go with you to the first floor.

01:18:21.988 --> 01:18:24.157
I heard the trailer for Wee-oww was out.

01:18:26.493 --> 01:18:28.704
What if all my fans rush here
after seeing this?

01:18:28.787 --> 01:18:30.372
Don't worry. There's only eight.

01:18:31.123 --> 01:18:31.957
Nine including you?

01:18:32.040 --> 01:18:32.999
Not me!

01:18:35.168 --> 01:18:37.129
But who will be the main character?

01:18:38.672 --> 01:18:39.756
Is it Yi-young?

01:18:41.091 --> 01:18:43.468
Yi-young, you delivered the baby
where the camera was.

01:18:43.552 --> 01:18:45.137
And you wanted to do the surgery.

01:18:45.220 --> 01:18:46.805
Forget it. It's embarrassing.

01:18:48.265 --> 01:18:50.475
Here it is.
"Trailer for Wee-oww Episode 1."

01:18:52.102 --> 01:18:54.813
A new era of human reality TV in 2023.

01:18:54.896 --> 01:18:56.440
Jang Yung-suk's Wee-oww.

01:18:57.149 --> 01:18:59.943
The place where you can never
let your guard down.

01:19:00.527 --> 01:19:02.070
Push harder! One last time!

01:19:02.154 --> 01:19:04.698
Were you waiting
until the fetal monitor signs dropped?

01:19:04.781 --> 01:19:06.324
Is your judgement that poor?

01:19:06.408 --> 01:19:09.536
A split second
can determine life or death.

01:19:09.619 --> 01:19:12.122
And those moments add up
to create a miracle!

01:19:12.873 --> 01:19:14.833
And it's where you meet beautiful people.

01:19:14.916 --> 01:19:16.126
Don't worry.

01:19:16.209 --> 01:19:17.878
You can ask me questions anytime.

01:19:18.420 --> 01:19:22.841
How could I ignore a mother
whose water just broke?

01:19:22.924 --> 01:19:25.761
She was lucky though.

01:19:26.344 --> 01:19:29.306
See for yourself
on Jang Yung-suk's Wee-oww.

01:19:35.270 --> 01:19:37.606
Myeong Eun-won again? Again?

01:19:37.689 --> 01:19:39.357
Why does everything good happen to her?

01:19:39.441 --> 01:19:40.525
Why?

01:19:41.485 --> 01:19:43.987
Hey, it's not her fault.

01:19:44.070 --> 01:19:45.572
Damn you, Jang.

01:19:46.782 --> 01:19:48.533
I'm never watching his shows again.

01:19:53.705 --> 01:19:55.665
Hey, did you see Yi-young's face?

01:19:56.958 --> 01:19:57.918
When was it?

01:19:58.001 --> 01:19:59.377
-At 17 seconds.
-It was?

01:20:02.923 --> 01:20:03.799
Going home?

01:20:06.343 --> 01:20:07.302
Did you see it?

01:20:07.385 --> 01:20:08.261
No.

01:20:09.638 --> 01:20:10.806
No what?

01:20:10.889 --> 01:20:11.723
What?

01:20:12.224 --> 01:20:13.433
What didn't you see?

01:20:21.566 --> 01:20:23.568
PLEASE DON'T PUSH THE DOOR

01:20:28.698 --> 01:20:29.825
Hey!

01:20:29.908 --> 01:20:30.784
Excuse me.

01:20:30.867 --> 01:20:32.118
Please be careful.

01:20:34.955 --> 01:20:35.914
Please go on.

01:21:21.668 --> 01:21:24.087
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUESTS,
NAH YUNG-SUK &amp; SHIN WON-HO,

01:21:24.170 --> 01:21:25.797
THE ETERNAL COMEDY DUO

01:21:25.881 --> 01:21:29.175
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:21:29.259 --> 01:21:31.469
-Don't they seem weird these days?
-In what way?

01:21:31.553 --> 01:21:32.512
It's a bloody rivalry.

01:21:32.596 --> 01:21:35.140
Did you tell Prof. Kong
the surgeries have been delayed?

01:21:35.223 --> 01:21:37.017
If we have two, I should get one.

01:21:37.100 --> 01:21:38.351
Why does she get both?

01:21:38.435 --> 01:21:39.561
I need that one.

01:21:39.644 --> 01:21:41.354
That's what I was going to say.

01:21:41.438 --> 01:21:42.647
I need it.

01:21:42.731 --> 01:21:44.316
Is she playing mind games with me?

01:21:44.399 --> 01:21:46.318
-It's Prof. Seo's patient.
-Hold on.

01:21:46.401 --> 01:21:47.611
Professor Kong said…

01:21:47.694 --> 01:21:50.280
You should come during lunch
when we're on break.

01:21:50.363 --> 01:21:52.073
I told you several times I just heard too.

01:21:52.824 --> 01:21:53.825
I'll be quick!

01:21:53.909 --> 01:21:54.743
Did you two fight?

01:21:54.826 --> 01:21:56.620
-No!
-You did.

01:21:56.703 --> 01:21:58.580
Why would I? I have no reason to.

01:21:58.663 --> 01:22:00.373
Are you in a contest to see who's worse?

01:22:01.499 --> 01:22:02.375
What?

01:22:02.459 --> 01:22:04.419
What are you going to do?
Get married? You?

01:22:04.502 --> 01:22:05.503
Who is it?

01:22:05.587 --> 01:22:06.588
Is it someone from work?

01:22:06.671 --> 01:22:09.132
Do you want to keep this a secret
or tell everyone?

01:22:09.215 --> 01:22:10.634
The first-years don't know anything.

01:22:10.717 --> 01:22:12.761
I wonder if I should tell them first.

01:22:12.844 --> 01:22:14.387
-Who was that?
-Are you…

01:22:15.388 --> 01:22:17.223
What are you doing?

01:22:17.307 --> 01:22:20.769
Are you here to save lives
or to take them?

01:22:20.852 --> 01:22:21.728
I'm sorry.

01:22:21.811 --> 01:22:24.147
If you want to be alone,
come here during the day.

01:22:24.230 --> 01:22:25.482
And go there at night.

01:22:26.024 --> 01:22:27.525
I haven't been here in so long. Gosh.

01:22:27.609 --> 01:22:30.028
We were both so young

01:22:30.111 --> 01:22:34.199
The foolish memories of my first love

01:22:34.991 --> 01:22:37.494
I hope this song

01:22:37.577 --> 01:22:41.998
Can send us back to those days

01:22:43.208 --> 01:22:47.087
When that day comes, I'll tell you then

01:22:47.170 --> 01:22:50.590
You were my whole life

01:22:50.674 --> 01:22:53.009
The end of longing

01:22:53.093 --> 01:22:54.594
When that day comes

01:22:54.678 --> 01:22:58.682
I'll come running to you

01:23:02.727 --> 01:23:06.147
If that fateful day ever comes

01:23:10.235 --> 01:23:13.029
I hope we can meet again

01:23:13.113 --> 01:23:15.323
I'll keep wishing on and on

01:23:17.409 --> 01:23:19.411
Subtitle translation by: Jamie Jin
